# ESP-IDF generates sdkconfig from sdkconfig.defaults, and the build tree is a
# build tree. Neither belongs in the repository: sdkconfig holds every default
# IDF chose for this host, which is exactly the kind of thing that turns into a
# mystery diff later.
sdkconfig
sdkconfig.old
build/
# And the radio's own build tree, which `scripts/esp32-proto.sh` keeps beside
# the default one so that the half of the port a real board uses is compiled
# without disturbing the half the checks run (see docs/17-esp32-port.md).
build-wifi/
